-- Hand-built, deliberately VALID instance of ZebraPuzzle.use (plain SOIL
-- statements -- !create/!set only, no association inserts since House has
-- none -- no Kodkod search involved). This is the unique solution of the
-- classic "Life International" Zebra Puzzle (first published in Life
-- International magazine, 17 December 1962; the exact 15-clue version this
-- .use file encodes, per ZebraPuzzle.use's own header), mapped one-to-one
-- onto this model's House class.
--
-- INDEPENDENCE FROM THE SOLVER: this instance was NOT taken from any
-- Kodkod/mv -validate run of this plugin. The Zebra Puzzle predates the
-- KK-ModelValidator plugin (and this entire repository) by over 60 years
-- and has exactly one well-known, independently-verifiable solution that
-- is solvable by pure hand logic -- that is the whole point of the puzzle,
-- and why it is a legitimate correctness oracle rather than a
-- self-consistency check. See docs/kk-modelvalidator-port.md for why an
-- independently-sourced fixture is required for the "validating" mode.
--
-- DERIVATION (re-worked by hand from the 14 clues, not merely copied from
-- memory of the famous answer, then cross-checked against it):
--   1) Clue10 -> house1 = Norwegian.
--   2) Clue15 -> house2 = Blue (Norwegian's only neighbor is house2).
--   3) Clue06 (Green = Ivory position + 1) combined with house2 already
--      being Blue rules out (Ivory,Green) = (1,2) and (2,3), leaving
--      (Ivory,Green) = (3,4) or (4,5).
--   4) Testing (Ivory,Green) = (4,5): remaining colors {Red,Yellow} go to
--      houses 1,3. If house1=Red, Clue02 (Englishman->Red) forces house1
--      to be Englishman -- but house1 is already Norwegian (step 1),
--      contradiction. So house1=Yellow, house3=Red, and Clue02 forces
--      house3=Englishman.
--   5) Clue08 (Yellow->Kools) -> house1 smokes Kools. Clue12 (Kools
--      adjacent Horse) -> house1's only neighbor, house2, has the Horse.
--   6) Clue09 -> house3 drinks Milk. Clue04 (Green->Coffee) -> house5
--      drinks Coffee. Remaining drinks {Water,Tea,OrangeJuice} go to
--      houses 1,2,4. Clue05 (Ukrainian->Tea): house5 already drinks
--      Coffee so house5 isn't Ukrainian; testing Ukrainian=house2 (drinks
--      Tea) leaves {Water,OrangeJuice} for houses 1,4. Clue13
--      (LuckyStrike->OrangeJuice): house1 already smokes Kools (step 5),
--      so house1 cannot be the LuckyStrike/OrangeJuice house -- forcing
--      house4=OrangeJuice+LuckyStrike and house1=Water.
--   7) Remaining nationalities {Spaniard,Japanese} go to houses 4,5.
--      Testing house4=Spaniard (Clue03: Spaniard->Dog, consistent with
--      house4 already fixed to LuckyStrike/OrangeJuice -- no clash),
--      house5=Japanese, so Clue14 (Japanese->Parliaments) -> house5
--      smokes Parliaments.
--   8) Remaining smokes {OldGold,Chesterfields} go to houses 2,3. House2
--      already has Horse (step 5) but Clue07 (OldGold->Snails) would
--      force Snails onto whichever house smokes OldGold -- house2 can't
--      be OldGold (already has Horse), so house3=OldGold (-> Snails, by
--      Clue07) and house2=Chesterfields.
--   9) Clue11 (Chesterfields adjacent Fox): house2's neighbors are
--      houses 1 and 3; house3 already has Snails (step 8), so the Fox
--      must be at house1.
--  10) Only Zebra is left unassigned, for the only house left, house5.
--
-- This reproduces, independently, the puzzle's universally published
-- answer: the Norwegian (house1) drinks Water, and the Japanese (house5)
-- owns the Zebra.
--
-- Every one of ZebraPuzzle.use's 22 invariants (PositionRange, the 6
-- DistinctXxx bijection invariants, the 14 original clues Clue02..Clue15,
-- and the derived corollary Clue16) was then hand-checked against this
-- exact assignment, one by one, and holds -- see valid-instance.cmd.

!create h1 : House
!set h1.position := 1
!set h1.color := #Yellow
!set h1.nationality := #Norwegian
!set h1.drink := #Water
!set h1.smoke := #Kools
!set h1.pet := #Fox

!create h2 : House
!set h2.position := 2
!set h2.color := #Blue
!set h2.nationality := #Ukrainian
!set h2.drink := #Tea
!set h2.smoke := #Chesterfields
!set h2.pet := #Horse

!create h3 : House
!set h3.position := 3
!set h3.color := #Red
!set h3.nationality := #Englishman
!set h3.drink := #Milk
!set h3.smoke := #OldGold
!set h3.pet := #Snails

!create h4 : House
!set h4.position := 4
!set h4.color := #Ivory
!set h4.nationality := #Spaniard
!set h4.drink := #OrangeJuice
!set h4.smoke := #LuckyStrike
!set h4.pet := #Dog

!create h5 : House
!set h5.position := 5
!set h5.color := #Green
!set h5.nationality := #Japanese
!set h5.drink := #Coffee
!set h5.smoke := #Parliaments
!set h5.pet := #Zebra
